>        "You feel more experienced. Welcome to experience level 0 <more>
>        Your fingertips glow white!"

That was one of the funny things in hack 1.0.3 - every number was
visibly encoded in a limited (small) number of bits. The fact that
experience only goes to 31 and then back to 0 can be used profitably,
though:
- create lots of potions of gain level (by polymorph, watch out, only
the top item on each position gets polymorphed)
- quaff until you have level 32 -> 0
- kill some monsters (by then, AC is usually below 0 and weapon ++, so
there's not much of a risk - not to mention the number of HP's)
this will make your experience level (and HP's) go up very fast (just a
few monsters to get to 7 or so)
- quaff the rest of the potions (make sure you get to level 10 or
higher)
It's a bit disappointing, though, when you drop 2 more diamonds on your
stack of 255, and I never let my HP's go above 1023 - I didn't dare.

